{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Battle resurrections: two per raid boss fight, refused after the last, restored by the next pull",
  "contract": [
    "Tester (ZG feedback, 2026-11-04): in-combat resurrections such as the Pyromancer's and Necromancer's are",
    "limited per fight, two up to a 15-player raid and three in a 25-player raid, with yellow text at the top of",
    "the screen. A resurrection cast in combat during a raid boss fight uses a charge and every player in the",
    "instance is told how many are left. With none left the cast is refused. A resurrection cast in combat",
    "outside a boss fight is free, and the next pull starts with full charges. A boss pulled while another boss",
    "fight goes on joins that fight and restores no charges. Druid Rebirth (20484) stands in",
    "for the class battle resurrections, which share its resurrection effect."
  ],
  "timeout_ms": 120000,
  "location": {
    "map": 0,
    "x": -8914.0,
    "y": -133.0,
    "z": 80.6
  },
  "players": [
